		/// <summary>Begin linking an SSO provider</summary>
		/// <remarks>
		/// <para>Starts Cognito federation for the named provider (google or apple) to link it to the caller's account, and returns the URL to send the browser to. The response sets the federation_state cookie the callback checks, so it must be requested from the browser that follows the URL. Open the popup the flow runs in before calling this, or the browser blocks it. The callback links the identity whatever its email, sends the outcome to the account's sockets as account.identity.linked or account.identity.link.failed (with the error code, such as identity_already_linked), and redirects the popup to the completion URL with link=&lt;provider&gt; either way. An account that already has an identity from the provider answers provider_already_linked here.</para>
		/// <para>Tags: users.</para>
		/// <para>Error codes (open: an unlisted code is still possible): 400 Bad Request: federation_provider_invalid. 401 Unauthorized: unauthorized. 409 Conflict: provider_already_linked. 500 Internal Server Error: internal_error. 503 Service Unavailable: federation_unavailable.</para>
